<title>FINLAND: Pohjola says completes Salama takeover.</title>
<headline>Pohjola says completes Salama takeover.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish insurer Pohjola said in a statement on Tuesday it had bought a total 99 percent of shares in Salama from mutual life insurers Suomi and A-Vakuutus, and pension insurer Ilmarinen for 578.2 million markka.</p>
<p>&quot;The purchase price will be adjusted on the basis of the forthcoming interim accounts to correspond to the changes in Salama's net asset value over the period January to June 30, 1997,&quot; Pohjola said.</p>
<p>The takeover is part of a life insurance reshuffle within the Pohjola group's sphere of influence.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
